    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the season, our optimization model leans heavily into matchups against vulnerable arms to secure counting stats, despite several high-end starters dotting today\u2019s slate. **Luis Lara** emerges as our strongest play at 52.40, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Ray (xERA 4.98). While hitting 7th, his switch-hitting versatility and the significant SP Skill advantage elevate him above the pack. **Kyle Tucker** (51.86) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (51.65) follow closely; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically benefits from a dynamic platoon edge against Rasmussen, mitigating the challenge of his 3.30 xERA. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** holds a stable 50.88 despite facing the formidable Misiorowski, as his projected output remains insulated by his premium spot in the order and a favorable platoon profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 36.43 score. Ultimately, the model pulled him back because he failed to clear our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" for active starts, largely due to a suppressed batting position (9th) and a challenging matchup against Smith. We are choosing to preserve game caps rather than force an underperforming asset. Conversely, we must monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin**, who sits at a 47.67 score despite a high-stakes duel with Skubal (2.85 xERA); the model favors his leadoff profile here, but he remains the most volatile asset in today's lineup given the quality of the opposing arm. We remain without **Luis Robert Jr.** due to his ongoing IL status, and with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** scheduled for an off-day, our depth\u2014including **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Nasim Nunez**\u2014must remain prepared to rotate in as we prioritize defensive efficiency and sprint speed across the diamond.",
